      .K.O i think have a solution. I've been giving it somethought,
      and everything seems doable. The one iffy thing is how to
      interete a bare reference to object in the first
      position of a list. There are a couple different
      ways to imahine it, but the big two is it a
      get or a send. My solution is to interprete this
      as a send. If using dot notation, those will be decomposed
      into intermeatary gets. To do a get, simply reverse
      the order  starting with the string key, just like
      with an index look up. This differey from a module load where there are
      no parameters. Multiple parameters are done recerusivly. So
      ("string" objects) -> object["string"]
      ("string1" "string2" object) -> object["string2"]["string1"]
